  "question": {
    "text": "For a first order reaction <math><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>B</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>)</mo></math> at constant volume and 300 K, the total pressure at the beginning <math><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and at time are <math><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math>, respectively. Initially, only A is present with concentration <math><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math>, and&nbsp; <math><msub><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#160;</mi></mrow></msub></math> is the time required for the partial pressure of A to reach <math><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></math> of its initial value. The correct option(s) is (are)<br />(Assume that all these gases behave as ideal gases)"
